course: dictionary
lesson: 13809
title: Irradiate: rays and light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To irradiate something is to send rays onto it or through it. Rays such as X-rays, gamma rays and ultraviolet light are often invisible, so you cannot always see them at work. «The doctor used X-rays to irradiate the broken arm and check the bones.»
explain: Irradiate has a second meaning, about food. «The factory will irradiate the strawberries to kill germs, so they stay fresh for longer.» The rays kill the germs, so the food keeps for longer. Irradiate is a verb, so it changes: irradiates, irradiated, irradiating.
explain: In a story, irradiate can mean to light something up brightly. «A huge smile irradiated her face.» No real rays are involved here. The writer is saying her face lit up with happiness. When you meet irradiate, look for clues about light, rays or brightness around it.
fact: Irradiate is a verb: irradiate, irradiates, irradiated, irradiating.
fact: To irradiate means to send rays, such as X-rays, gamma rays or ultraviolet light, onto or through something.
fact: To irradiate food means to treat it with rays to kill germs so it lasts longer.
fact: In a story, irradiate can mean to light something up brightly, as in «The morning sun irradiated the hills with gold.»
fact: Doctors can irradiate cancer cells to kill them.
exercise: «The factory will irradiate the apples to kill germs.» What does irradiate mean here? | Pack them into boxes | Paint them bright red | Peel and slice into pieces | *Treat with rays to kill germs
exercise: «Her smile irradiated the whole room.» What does irradiate suggest? | Made the room colder | Shouted loudly | Hid from view | *Lit up brightly
exercise: «Scientists irradiated the seeds yesterday.» Which word shows that this happened in the past? | irradiate | irradiating | irradiates | *irradiated
test: What does irradiate mean in «The lab will irradiate the sample with ultraviolet light»? | Weigh it carefully | Mix it with water | *Shine rays onto it | Cool it down in a freezer
test: Which sentence uses irradiate to mean lit up brightly? | «The factory will irradiate the milk to kill germs.» | *«The morning sun irradiated the hills with gold.» | «The doctor will irradiate the cells.» | «The cook will irradiate the lettuce.»
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to irradiate when it means to light something up? | Sleep | Chop | *Illuminate | Freeze
